cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or workflow, please cite the Adaptive-QMB repository and the associated manuscript when available."
title: "Adaptive-QMB: Reproducible ACT-QMB Workflow for CMIP6 Rainfall Bias Correction"
type: software
version: "1.2.4"
authors:
  - family-names: "Hidayati"
    given-names: "Fitria"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4789-7305"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hidayatihub/Adaptive-QMB"
keywords:
  - rainfall bias correction
  - Quantile Matching Bootstrap
  - Quantile Delta Mapping
  - CMIP6
  - precipitation extremes
  - climate model post-processing
abstract: >-
  Adaptive-QMB is the publication-facing repository for the ACT-QMB method,
  providing a reproducible R workflow for adaptive upper-tail rainfall bias
  correction of CMIP6 daily precipitation. The repository contains the
  publication-facing QMB baseline, ACT-QMB core, common metric engine,
  inferential comparison runner, validation utilities, and figure-generation
  code used in the major-revision analysis.
